<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakhstan, Japan to set up air links.</title>
<headline>Kazakhstan, Japan to set up air links.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The aviation authorities of Kazakhstan and Japan plan to start regular flights between the new Kazakh capital of Akmola and Tokyo, a spokesman for the Kazakh prime minister said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Amirzhan Kosanov said that the new route would aid the &quot;development of links between the two countries&quot;. He gave no further details.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, (3272) 509410</p>
